  "title": "Object slicing",
  "chapter": "05-inheritance",
  "summary": "Slide 124: assigning a Cercle to a Forme copies only the Forme part. Pointers and references keep the whole object.",
  "code": "struct Forme  { virtual ~Forme() = default; Point centre_; };\nstruct Cercle : Forme { int rayon_; };\n\nint main() {\n  Cercle c{ { 9, 9 }, 3 };\n  Forme  f{ { 0, 0 } };\n  f = c;               // slicing\n  Forme *pf{ &c };     // no slicing\n  Forme &rf{ c };      // no slicing\n}",
